course: dictionary
lesson: 6676
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «The object of the game is to score goals.» Here object means the aim or purpose of the game, not a thing you can hold.
explain: «The bag was full of objects: a pen, a key and a shell.» Here an object is a thing you can see and touch that is not alive. Say OB-ject for the noun, but ob-JECT for the verb, as in «I object to that rule».
explain: Grammar uses object too. In «Sam kicked the ball», the ball is the object, because it is the thing the kick acts on. To check any meaning, swap it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Object (noun, OB-ject) means a thing you can see and touch that is not alive.
fact: Object can also mean a purpose or aim, as in «the object of the game».
fact: In grammar, the object is the word for the thing or person that the verb acts on.
fact: Object pronouns are me, him, her, us and them, as in «Mum gave sweets to Ben and me».
fact: To object (verb, ob-JECT) means to say you disagree or do not like something.
exercise: «The object of the game is to score goals.» What does object mean here? | *An aim or purpose | A thing you can hold | A loud noise | A kind of ball
exercise: In «Sam kicked the ball», which word is the object? | kicked | Sam kicked | Sam | *the ball
exercise: Dad says, «I object to muddy boots on the sofa.» What does object mean? | To pick something up very fast | To hide under a table | To buy something new | *To say you disagree or do not like it
test: Which word means a thing you can see and touch that is not alive? | Dream | Wind | Idea | *Stone
test: «Mum gave sweets to Ben and me.» Which word is an object pronoun? | I | we | they | *me
exam: «Memory games train your attention: look at the objects on a tray, then name them.» What does objects mean? | Bright lights | Aims or purposes | Ways of disagreeing | *Things you can see and touch
